RLVM: include the directory definitions used by the system file cache.

The removed convenience header is not used for convenience functions here.
Path operations already have direct headers; directory traversal requires
its current owning header. Keep file-cache/save-directory behavior unchanged.
Upstream RLVM copyright and GPL-3.0-or-later notices remain unchanged.

diff --git a/src/systems/base/system.cc b/src/systems/base/system.cc
--- a/src/systems/base/system.cc
+++ b/src/systems/base/system.cc
@@ -30,3 +30,3 @@
 #include <boost/algorithm/string.hpp>
-#include <boost/filesystem/convenience.hpp>
+#include <boost/filesystem/directory.hpp>
 #include <boost/filesystem/operations.hpp>
